Conclusion--

-- Today I learned that gesture recognition goes one step beyond hand tracking. While hand tracking detects the position of the user's hands and fingers, gesture recognition interprets 
specific hand poses and movements as commands. This enables users to interact with XR applications naturally, making virtual experiences more intuitive and immersive.
